<p>greater, since taking the calorimeter&rsquo;s heat capacity into account will compensate for the thermal energy transferred to the solution from the calorimeter; this approach includes the calorimeter itself, along with the solution, as &ldquo;surroundings&rdquo;: <em>q</em><sub>rxn</sub> = &minus;(<em>q</em><sub>solution</sub> + <em>q</em><sub>calorimeter</sub>); since both <em>q</em><sub>solution</sub> and <em>q</em><sub>calorimeter</sub> are negative, including the latter term (<em>q</em><sub>rxn</sub>) will yield a greater value for the heat of the dissolution</p>

